 This AMENDED AND RESTATED LIMITED LIABILITY COMPANY AGREEMENT OF [Name of Asset LLC]  (this “Agreement”), dated as of [date] (the “Effective Date”), at 9:05 a.m. (the “Effective Time”), is adopted, executed, and agreed to, for good and valuable consideration, by [name of Sponsor], a [type of entity] (the “Sponsor”), and [Name of Transferor], a [type of entity] (the  “Transferor”).  This Agreement is also executed by Hawaii I 125-0 Trust, a Delaware business trust (the “Trust”), for the purpose of agreeing to the provisions hereof as a Class B Member and the transferee of the Transferor, from and after the Closing Time (as herein defined).


RECITALS

 1. [Name of Asset LLC] (the “Company”) was formed as a Delaware limited liability company on [date] (the “Formation Date”), by the filing of a Certificate of Formation (the “Delaware Certificate”) with the Delaware Secretary of State, and the Sponsor was admitted to the Company as the initial Member, effective as of the Formation Date, pursuant to that certain Limited Liability Company Agreement dated as of the Formation Date (the “Original Agreement”).

 2. The Sponsor, the Transferor and the Trust now desire to amend and restate the Original Agreement in its entirety and, in connection therewith, to evidence the admission of the Trust as a Member.

 3. At the Closing Time, on the Effective Date, but after the Effective Time, it is the intention of the Transferor to Dispose of its Class B Member Interest in the Company to the Trust by executing the B Interest Assignment and otherwise complying with the terms of the Transfer and Auction Agreement.

 4 . It is the intention of the Members that the Trust, as the transferee of the Transferor’s Class B Member Interest, will be admitted as a Member of the Company from and after the Closing Time.

 NOW THEREFORE, for good and valuable consideration, the Sponsor, the Transferor, and the Trust hereby amend and restate the Original Agreement as follows:

