ross negligence, willful misconduct or fraud could not have known of, the material misstatement or omission.  The Managing Member shall devote such time and effort to the Company business and operations as the Managing Member deems necessary to promote fully the interests of the Company; however, the Managing Member is not required to devote full time to Company business.  In no event shall the provisions of this Section 6.02 relieve the Managing Member from liability pursuant to the provisions of any contract or transaction that may be entered into hereafter between the Company and the Managing Member.  The Managing Member shall owe no fiduciary duties to the Company or the Class B Member, other than as set forth above.

